Package: treeAIBoxR
Type: Package
Title: R-Native Wood/Foliage Classification Using TreeAIBox Weights
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Andrew", "G.", role = c("aut", "cre"),
                  email = "andrew@example.invalid")
Description: Pure-R port of the voxelized 3D SegFormer architecture used
    in NRCan's TreeAIBox plugin (Xi, Hopkinson & Chasmer 2018; Xi,
    Chasmer & Hopkinson 2023). Loads the official TreeAIBox PyTorch
    state dicts via the R 'torch' package and runs inference on per-tree
    point clouds without requiring Python, CloudCompare, or PyTorch.
    Distributed for non-commercial research use; pretrained weights are
    licensed CC BY-NC 4.0 by NRCan.
License: GPL (>= 2)
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.2)
Imports:
    torch (>= 0.13.0),
    data.table,
    R6,
    jsonlite,
    igraph,
    mclust,
    Rcpp (>= 1.0.0)
LinkingTo:
    Rcpp,
    BH
Suggests:
    testthat
RoxygenNote: 7.3.2
SystemRequirements: A CPU build of libtorch is sufficient. CUDA is
    optional and only used if torch::cuda_is_available() returns TRUE.
